&#8220;Me and Bey have known each other since we were 8 and 9 years old. Now we&#8217;re in our 40s with children,&#8221; Rowland said. &#8220;The relationship became richer with Michelle. It&#8217;s so rich. Time really gives you a richness and a strength and a bond in the relationship.

The 45-year-old continued: &#8220;When people see us together, they&#8217;re kind of shocked because sometimes, especially girl groups, that was there for that time, but honey, we here for the long haul. When we said that kind of &#8216;I do&#8217; with each other, it&#8217;s like, &#8216;Oh no, no, I&#8217;m here through thick and thin. That&#8217;s a friendship type of marriage situation.&#8221;

Destiny&#8217;s Child&#8217;s last reunion came when Rowland and Williams joined Beyoncé in Las Vegas at the finale of her Cowboy Carter Tour for a surprise appearance in Las Vegas.

The July 2025 show at Allegiant Stadium marked their first performance in seven years, as the trio ran through a medley that included &#8220;Lose My Breath&#8221; and &#8220;Independent Women.&#8221;

One of the most influential girl groups shaping contemporary R&B, Destiny&#8217;s Child released five albums, the last of which, Destiny Fulfilled , arrived in 2004, and peaked at No. 2 on the Billboard 200.

DC notched four No. 1 hits on the Billboard Hot 100, including &#8220;Say My Name,&#8221; &#8220;Bills, Bills, Bills,&#8221; &#8220;Independent Woman&#8221; and &#8220;Bootylicious.&#8221;

